{
  "_readme": [
    "CANONICAL GEOGRAPHY FOR THE CROVIA PILOT. Single source of truth.",
    "The Expo app, the FastAPI backend and the simulation all read THIS file.",
    "Do not duplicate coordinates anywhere else.",
    "",
    "ZONE RADIUS IS 600 m, NOT 450 m.",
    "Nokia advised that geofence accuracy works at cell-tower level, that 600 m",
    "is the smallest usable radius, and that smaller areas give inconsistent",
    "results. Two consequences follow, and both are deliberate:",
    "",
    "  1. There are 5 zones, not 6. At 600 m the old Boulevard zone sat only",
    "     519 m from the tram link zone, so the two circles would have covered",
    "     almost the same ground while being billed twice. The Boulevard is",
    "     still watched, at district level, inside district_stadium.",
    "",
    "  2. Every segment chain starts and ends OUTSIDE its 600 m circle, so a",
    "     crowd genuinely crosses the boundary in both directions.",
    "",
    "Segment offsets are metres east (x) and north (y) from the zone centre.",
    "Width is what decides throughput; length only decides how many people fit."
  ],
